# Bucket Policy (Account B — 222222222222)

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {
        "AWS": "arn:aws:iam::111111111111:root"
      },
      "Action": [
        "s3:GetObject",
        "s3:ListBucket"
      ],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::shared-data",
        "arn:aws:s3:::shared-data/*"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

Bucket: shared-data
Account: 222222222222

# Alice's IAM Policy (Account A — 111111111111)

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "s3:ListAllMyBuckets",
        "s3:GetBucketLocation"
      ],
      "Resource": "*"
    }
  ]
}
```

Note: Alice's IAM policy does NOT include `s3:GetObject` or `s3:ListBucket` for the shared-data bucket. The bucket policy allows Account A's root, but Alice needs her own IAM Allow too.
